blocks:
- discriminant: innerHero
  value:
    title: Odoo Fixed-Price Development
    subTitle: A fixed price, a written scope, a date. You know what you're paying before you start.
    bottomLine: true
    image: banner-bg-3.svg
- discriminant: textSection
  value:
    title: Why time-and-materials doesn't work for you
    content: '<p>With time-and-materials, you sign an hourly rate and an estimate. If the project slips, the bill follows. You alone carry the risk of an estimate you didn''t make.</p><p>It''s the industry''s standard model, and that''s exactly why many business owners give up on genuinely useful developments: the uncertainty costs more than the project itself.</p>'
    emphasis: false
- discriminant: methodologies
  value:
    bgClass: white-bg
    title: How we work
    description: ''
    methodologies:
    - heading: Scoping (billed, a few days)
      description: <p>We write down together exactly what needs to be built, down to the screens. This document is yours, even if you don't go further.</p>
    - heading: Fixed price
      description: <p>From the scoping document, we commit to an amount and a date. Not a range.</p>
    - heading: Development
      description: <p>We deliver in stages, you validate as we go.</p>
    - heading: Guarantee
      description: <p>What we build stays compatible with Odoo updates, under the maintenance contract.</p>
- discriminant: textSection
  value:
    title: What the fixed price doesn't cover
    content: <p>The fixed price applies to development whose scope is written down. It doesn't cover day-to-day support, ongoing hand-holding, or scope changes decided mid-project — those go through a priced amendment using the same method.</p><p>We don't take on a project without prior scoping, and we don't take over existing development without an audit.</p>
    emphasis: true
- discriminant: forfaitCases
  value:
    title: Three examples
    intro: Typical projects, compared with what they would have cost on a time-and-materials basis.
    note: Anonymised examples and indicative amounts (excl. VAT) — every project is priced after scoping.
    labels:
      context: Context
      need: Need
      regie: Time & materials (est.)
      forfait: Fixed price
      result: Result
    cases:
    - sector: Kitchen retailer
      context: Kitchen retailer that designs projects in Carat and runs the business in Odoo.
      need: Connector between the Carat quoting software and Odoo.
      regie: €12,000
      forfait: €5,000
      delay: ''
      result: Carat quotes land directly in Odoo, with no re-keying.
    - sector: Property management
      context: Agency managing around 200 properties, charges and statements handled by hand.
      need: Owner and tenant portal with charge statements generated from Odoo.
      regie: €22,000 – 30,000
      forfait: €14,800
      delay: 8 weeks
      result: Statements sent automatically, fewer requests to the front desk.
    - sector: Retail
      context: Shop with a point of sale and stock tracked across several tools.
      need: Mobile app for order taking and stock control, connected to Odoo.
      regie: €15,000 – 20,000
      forfait: €9,800
      delay: 5 weeks
      result: Real-time stock, orders entered only once.
- discriminant: textSection
  value:
    title: 'Odoo driven by AI: the MCP protocol'
    content: '<p>MCP (Model Context Protocol) is the standard that lets an AI such as Claude or ChatGPT connect directly to your Odoo. The AI no longer guesses: it reads your real data, with the permissions you define.</p><ul><li>Query your data in plain language: "Which customers have an invoice more than 30 days overdue?"</li><li>Generate reports and summaries (sales, stock, margins) without an Excel export</li><li>Trigger actions from a simple request: prepare a quote, create a task, update a record</li><li>Stay in control: the AI acts with the access of an Odoo user, and you choose what it can read or change</li></ul><p>We set up the connection, define the AI''s scope with you and build, at a fixed price, the custom tools it needs.</p>'
    emphasis: false
- discriminant: textSection
  value:
    title: Screens your teams actually want to use
    content: '<p>A poorly designed ERP gets bypassed: people go back to Excel and you lose the benefit of the project. We treat usability as part of development, not as a finishing touch.</p>'
    emphasis: false
